87.09960579872133,
167.48238372802737
],
"fontSize": 25.185540318489103
},
{
"text": "cute coronary syndrome remains one of the leading",
"rect": [
83.44726860523224,
157.32617247104645,
291.60156548023224,
167.32617187499997
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953524
},
{
"text": "causes of morbidity and mortality globally despite ad-",
"rect": [
83.44726860523224,
145.34377920627597,
291.59180223941803,
155.3437786102295
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953524
},
{
"text": "vances in primary and secondary preventive treatments",
"rect": [
71.93359136581421,
133.29300749301913,
291.6211009025574,
143.29300689697266
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953524
},
{
"text": "(1). Histologic and intravascular imaging investigations",
"rect": [
71.93359136581421,
121.31053376197815,
291.6601538658142,
131.31054210662845
],
"fontSize": 10.000008344650297
},
{
"text": "have demonstrated that most cases of acute coronary",
"rect": [
71.93359136581421,
109.33787691593167,
291.6211009025574,
119.33787631988527
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953595
},
{
"text": "syndrome are due to the rupture of large and lipid-rich",
"rect": [
71.93359136581421,
97.3554836511612,
291.6699171066285,
107.35548305511472
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953524
},
{
"text": "atheromas (2). Thus, the early, accurate identification",
"rect": [
71.93359136581421,
85.30471193790436,
291.6601538658142,
95.3047113418579
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953538
},
{
"text": "of these high-risk vulnerable plaques is of importance.",
"rect": [
71.93359136581421,
73.32224714756006,
291.6796803474426,
83.32224655151367
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953609
},
{
"text": "Gray-scale intravascular US can provide a unique op-",
"rect": [
71.93359136581421,
61.34958136081689,
291.6308641433716,
71.3495807647705
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953602
},
{
"text": "portunity to visualize vulnerable plaque features, in-",
"rect": [
71.93359136581421,
49.37691557407372,
291.6699171066285,
59.37691497802732
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953602
},
{
"text": "cluding attenuated plaque and echolucent plaque (3).",
"rect": [
71.93359136581421,
37.31641638278958,
291.6796803474426,
47.31641578674319
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953609
},
{
"text": "These features have been reported to be associated with",
"rect": [
71.93359136581421,
25.343750596046412,
291.6406273841858,
35.343750000000014
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953602
},
{
"text": "worse clinical outcomes (4,5). However, intravascular",
"rect": [
308.7597727775574,
157.32617247104645,
528.466808795929,
167.32617187499997
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953524
},
{
"text": "US is an invasive, expensive technique and is not widely",
"rect": [
308.7597727775574,
145.34377920627597,
528.466808795929,
155.3437786102295
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953524
},
{
"text": "available in most laboratories.",
"rect": [
308.7597727775574,
133.29300749301913,
426.58204436302185,
143.29300689697266
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953524
},
{
"text": "Coronary CT angiography (CCTA) is now a first-line",
"rect": [
320.75196504592896,
121.31053376197815,
528.4765720367432,
131.31054210662845
],
"fontSize": 10.000008344650297
},
{
"text": "noninvasive imaging modality for diagnosing coronary ar-",
"rect": [
308.7597727775574,
109.33787691593167,
528.5253882408142,
119.33787631988527
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953595
},
{
"text": "tery disease (CAD). Recently, qualitative plaque features",
"rect": [
308.7597727775574,
97.3554836511612,
528.4570455551147,
107.35548305511472
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953524
},
{
"text": "and quantitative attenuation-based plaque metrics at CCTA",
"rect": [
308.7597727775574,
85.30471193790436,
528.515625,
95.3047113418579
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953538
},
{
"text": "have demonstrated prognostic value for acute coronary syn-",
"rect": [
308.7597727775574,
73.32224714756006,
528.466808795929,
83.32224655151367
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953609
},
{
"text": "drome (6–8). However, these conventional anatomic CCTA",
"rect": [
308.7597727775574,
61.34958136081689,
528.515625,
71.3495807647705
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953602
},
{
"text": "parameters neglect the heterogeneity and spatial complexity",
"rect": [
308.7597727775574,
49.37691557407372,
528.466808795929,
59.37691497802732
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953602
},
{
"text": "in plaques. Previous studies have shown that the anatomic",
"rect": [
308.7597727775574,
37.31641638278958,
528.515625,
47.31641578674319
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953609
},
{
"text": "plaque features at CCTA had only a modest correlation with",
"rect": [
308.7597727775574,
25.343750596046412,
528.5351693630219,
35.343750000000014
],
"fontSize": 9.999999403953602
},
{
"text": "Background:",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
434.2500107288361,
115.44922292232513,
442.2480540275574
],
"fontSize": 7.998043298721257
},
{
"text": "A noninvasive coronary CT angiography (CCTA)–based radiomics technique may facilitate the identification of",
"rect": [
123.92578125,
433.83006620407104,
491.0351514816284,
442.32615995407104
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "vulnerable plaques and patients at risk for future adverse events.",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
424.357433795929,
292.6171839237213,
432.853527545929
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "Purpose:",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
402.6191489696503,
106.24023377895355,
410.6171922683716
],
"fontSize": 7.998043298721257
},
{
"text": "To assess whether a CCTA-based radiomic signature (RS) of vulnerable plaques defined with intravascular US was",
"rect": [
114.3164098262787,
402.2773461341858,
487.44140267372137,
410.7734398841858
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "associated with increased risk for future major adverse cardiac events (MACE).",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
392.7265720367432,
340.8496141433716,
401.2226657867432
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "Materials and Methods:",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
371.07615637779236,
144.74609792232513,
379.07419967651373
],
"fontSize": 7.99804329872137
},
{
"text": "In a retrospective study, an RS of vulnerable plaques was developed and validated using intravascular US as",
"rect": [
153.1347692012787,
370.65624761581427,
502.7245938777924,
379.15234136581427
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "the reference standard. The RS development data set included patients first undergoing CCTA and then intravascular US within",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
361.18357944488525,
503.8769602775574,
369.67967319488525
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "3 months between June 2013 and December 2020 at one tertiary hospital. The development set was randomly assigned to training",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
351.6328053474426,
511.93360090255743,
360.1288990974427
],
"fontSize": 8.496093750000057
},
{
"text": "and validation sets at a 7:3 ratio. Diagnostic performance was assessed internally and externally from three tertiary hospitals using",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
342.1601371765137,
507.3046803474426,
350.6562309265137
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "the area under the curve (AUC). The prognostic value of the RS for predicting MACE was evaluated in a prospective cohort with",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
332.6875047683716,
506.8554639816285,
341.1835985183716
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "suspected coronary artery disease between April 2018 and March 2019. Multivariable Cox regression analysis was used to evaluate",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
323.136730670929,
509.2968821525574,
331.632824420929
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "the RS and conventional anatomic plaque features (eg, segment involvement score) for predicting MACE.",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
313.6640625,
430.8203101158142,
322.16015625
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "Results:",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
292.0136826038361,
103.95508110523224,
300.0117259025574
],
"fontSize": 7.998043298721257
},
{
"text": "The RS development data set included 419 lesions from 225 patients (mean age, 64 years ± 10 [SD]; 68 men), while the",
"rect": [
112.41211295127869,
291.59373807907104,
506.37694001197815,
300.08983182907104
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "prognostic cohort included 1020 lesions from 708 patients (mean age, 62 years ± 11; 498 men). Sixteen radiomic features, includ-",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
282.121105670929,
510.7031464576721,
290.617199420929
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "ing two shape features and 14 textural features, were selected to build the RS. The RS yielded a moderate to good AUC in the",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
272.5703315734863,
495.2929615974426,
281.0664253234863
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "training, validation, internal, and external test sets (AUC = 0.81, 0.75, 0.80, and 0.77, respectively). A high RS (≥1.07) was inde-",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
263.0976634025574,
507.55859613418585,
271.5937571525574
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "pendently associated with MACE over a median 3-year follow-up (hazard ratio, 2.01;",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
253.54688930511472,
363.29101324081427,
262.04298305511475
],
"fontSize": 8.496093750000028
},
{
"text": "P",
"rect": [
365.2050733566284,
253.54688930511472,
369.93163526058197,
262.04298305511475
],
"fontSize": 8.496093750000028
},
{
"text": "= .005).",
"rect": [
372.0312595367432,
253.54688930511472,
398.1250047683716,
262.04298305511475
],
"fontSize": 8.496093750000028
},
{
"text": "Conclusion:",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
231.8867104053497,
112.50976324081422,
239.88475370407107
],
"fontSize": 7.99804329872137
},
{
"text": "A coronary CT angiography–derived radiomic signature of coronary plaque enabled the detection of vulnerable plaques",
"rect": [
120.95704078674316,
231.47656488418576,
512.7050757408142,
239.97265863418576
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
"text": "that were associated with increased risk for future adverse cardiac outcomes.",
"rect": [
83.92578363418579,
222.00389671325684,
331.6699147224426,
230.49999046325684
],
"fontSize": 8.49609375
},
{
